@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title DRAFT - C4 System Context (ADR-001)
rectangle "CSKH\nExternal system" as CSKH
rectangle "Reporting Consumer\nScoped external caller" as R
rectangle "Local Identity Provider\nOutside Telecom; JWT + JWKS" as IdP
rectangle "TelecomManagement\nSubscriber and financial backend" as T
CSKH --> T : business REST + JWT
R --> T : scoped consumption query
IdP ..> T : JWKS; issuer/audience verification
note bottom of T
  No real telecom network or payment integration.
  Database, broker, cache and scheduler are internal.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title DRAFT - C4 Containers (accepted technology choices; M3 pending)
rectangle "External CSKH / Reporting" as Clients
rectangle "Local external Identity Provider" as IdP
rectangle "TelecomManagement boundary" {
  rectangle "Spring Boot / Java21 backend\nAPI + internal jobs + UC01 recovery" as API
  database "PostgreSQL\nAuthoritative business state" as DB
  queue "RabbitMQ\nNumber-pool wake-up signal" as MQ
  database "Redis\nPackage catalog read cache; TTL60s" as Cache
}
rectangle "k6 load / reconciliation tools" as Tools
Clients --> API : REST / JWT
IdP ..> API : JWKS verification
API --> DB : JPA CRUD / JDBC with reason\ntransaction + uniqueness
API --> MQ : publish after stock commit
MQ --> API : idempotent consumer wake-up
API --> Cache : cache-aside / invalidate\nfallback to DB
Tools --> API : independent business test requests
Tools --> DB : controlled seed / reconciliation read
note bottom of API
  Recovery scans DB every60s if signal is lost.
  DB enforces FIFO, request ownership and expiry.
  No cache authority for balance, number or request IDs.
  Exact module/transaction/config review remains M3/M4.
end note
@enduml
